  Now the thing that actually matters: are the degree-1 Walsh coefficients
  of e^2 recovered? Those are what a folded-spectrum gradient needs.

  deg1 of <H>   exact [-0.5339  1.2741 -0.6349  0.1318]
                meas  [-0.5546  1.1991 -0.5734  0.1246]
    cos = 0.99923   norm ratio = 0.9473
